    &lt;div class=&quot;field-items&quot;&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;field-item odd&quot;&gt;
                      &lt;div class=&quot;field-label-inline-first&quot;&gt;
              Computer:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
                    Usaré mi portátil MacOSX        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/fieldset&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In English.  I will demo and describe how you can make beautiful maps with the &lt;a href=&quot;http://drupal.org/project/openlayers&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;Drupal OpenLayers module&lt;/a&gt;, specifically with the (still being developed) 2.x branch that has some great new features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://openlayers.org/&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;OpenLayers&lt;/a&gt; is a free, open-source Javascript library that allows for the presentation of mapping data within a website.  The Drupal OpenLayers modules provides an API to build, store, and present maps easily from the Drupal interface.&lt;/p&gt;
